userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add `GateRunStatus`, `GateRunRecord`, `classifyGateExit` and `gateOutputTail` to `src/finish/gates/quality.ts`, export `GATE_ORDER`, re-export all of them from `src/finish/index.ts`, and add the optional `onGate` callback to `runQualityGates`'s options.

**Motivation** — `runQualityGates` returns `{ passed, ran, failing, output }`, where `failing` lumps a 127 with a real test failure and per-gate exit codes exist only as `[<name>] exit=<n>` headers inside the combined `output` text; a caller wanting `not-run` vs `failed` would have to parse that text, and a per-gate record removes the parse.

**Approach** — `runQualityGates` builds one record per gate from the `QualityCommandResult` that decided it (the setup result when setup failed, otherwise the command result) and passes it to `onGate`. When `onGate` is given it is called exactly once per gate, synchronously, after that gate finishes and before the next gate starts, in run order. An exception thrown by `onGate` propagates out of `runQualityGates`. The returned `QualityGateResult` (`{ passed, ran, failing, output }`) is byte-for-byte what it is today, with or without `onGate`: a `not-run` or `timed-out` gate is still in `failing`. `runGateSetup` (`quality.ts`, file-local, baseline returns the failure chunk string or `null`) is free to change shape so `runQualityGates` can build a `GateRunRecord` from the setup's `QualityCommandResult` when the setup fails; the failure chunk written to `output` is unchanged. `GATE_ORDER` (baseline file-local `const GATE_ORDER = ["build", "typecheck", "lint", "test", "e2e"] as const`) keeps the same value but is exported and re-exported from `src/finish/index.ts`.

`classifyGateExit` rules, applied in this order: `timedOut === true` -> `timed-out`; `exitCode === 0` -> `passed`; `exitCode` is `127`, `126` or `-1` -> `not-run`; any other exit code -> `failed`.

Quality command facts: a timeout returns `exitCode: -1, timedOut: true`; a spawn error returns `exitCode: -1, timedOut: false`; a shell that cannot find or execute the command returns 127 or 126; a list-valued spec reports the first non-zero exit code (`aggregateResults`).

**Scope** — In: the new types/functions, the `GATE_ORDER` export, barrel re-exports, the `onGate` option, unchanged `QualityGateResult`. Out: the `nax gates run` CLI command and its report (US-002); the workflow's `runRepoGates` does not adopt `GateRunStatus`.

**Interface**
```typescript
export type GateRunStatus = "passed" | "failed" | "not-run" | "timed-out";

export interface GateRunRecord {
  /** The GateCommand name: "build", "test", ... */
  readonly name: string;
  /** Absolute directory the command was spawned from. */
  readonly cwd: string;
  readonly status: GateRunStatus;
  /** The exit code that decided the status: -1 for a single command's timeout or spawn error; for a list-valued command, the first non-zero step's code. */
  readonly exitCode: number;
  readonly durationMs: number;
  /** Present, as "setup", only when the gate's setup bootstrap failed and the command never ran. */
  readonly failedPhase?: "setup";
  /** The raw output of whichever run decided the status (setup or command). */
  readonly output: string;
}

/** The status for one QualityCommandResult. */
export function classifyGateExit(res: { readonly exitCode: number; readonly timedOut: boolean }): GateRunStatus;

/** The last `lines` lines of `output` after trailing newlines are removed, joined with "\n"; "" when nothing is left. */
export function gateOutputTail(output: string, lines?: number): string; // lines defaults to 40

// runQualityGates opts target:
// opts: { timeoutMs?: number; onGate?: (record: GateRunRecord) => void }
```
All of these are exported from `src/finish/gates/quality.ts` and re-exported from `src/finish/index.ts`, together with `GATE_ORDER`.

**Goal** — Add `src/cli/gates.ts` with `gatesRunCommand`, `registerGatesCommand`, `_gatesCliDeps` and the report types, following the `src/cli/workflow.ts` pattern; register it in `bin/nax.ts` next to `registerWorkflowCommand(program)`, re-export it from `src/cli/index.ts`, and add a `### nax gates run` section to the repo-root `docs/guides/cli-reference.md` (outside the package workdir) describing the flags, the four statuses and the exit codes.

**Motivation** — The nax-finish skill's Step 6 runs the gates by hand and one finish session reported gates as having run when a zsh shell loop returned exit 127 for every gate; nax already does all of this correctly in `runQualityGates` but has no CLI entry to it.

**Approach** — `nax gates run [-d, --dir <path>] [--gate <name>]... [--json]`. The command is mode-independent: it reads config and runs commands, touching no workflow or PRD state.

- `-d, --dir <path>` (default `process.cwd()`): any directory inside the project. `naxDir = findProjectDir(dir)`. When `naxDir` is `null`, or `realOrRaw(naxDir)` equals `realOrRaw(globalConfigDir())`, there is no project `.nax/config.json` at or above `dir` and the command fails with `no nax project found at or above <dir>`. Otherwise `projectDir = await normalizeTrustPath(dirname(naxDir))`; every later step (trust, `resolveGateCommands`, `runQualityGates`, the report's `projectDir`) uses that value. `realOrRaw` is imported from `@nathapp/nax-agent/internal`. Do not call `resolveTrustRoot`.
- `--gate <name>`: repeatable. Each value must be one of `build`, `typecheck`, `lint`, `test`, `e2e` (validate against the exported `GATE_ORDER`). Gates run in `GATE_ORDER` whatever order the flags were given in, and a repeated value runs once. A value outside that list fails with `unknown gate <name>; expected one of build, typecheck, lint, test, e2e`. A known gate that the project does not configure fails with `gate <name> is not configured; configured gates: <names>` (`configured gates: none` when there are none). No gate runs in either case.
- `--json`: stdout carries exactly one JSON document, the `GatesRunReport`, or `{"error": "<message>"}` when the command fails before reporting. Nothing else is written to stdout.
- Trust: before any config is loaded or command spawned, the command calls `ensureProjectTrusted(projectDir, { interactive })`, where `interactive` is `deps.isInteractive()` and `--json` is not set. `PROJECT_UNTRUSTED` fails the command with the two lines `Project not trusted: <projectDir>` and the error's `context.hint` (or `run: nax trust add <projectDir>` when the hint is absent); `TRUST_STORE_UNREADABLE` fails it with the error's message. Do NOT call `runTrustGate` (it exits the process with code 2; here an untrusted project is exit 1).
- Validation order, each step running only when every earlier one passed: (1) every `--gate` value is a known gate key (pure, no I/O); (2) project root resolution; (3) trust; (4) `resolveGateCommands(projectDir, [])`; (5) every `--gate` value is configured; (6) the gates run. A failure at any step returns before the next step starts.
- Sequence: the gates run one at a time, through `runQualityGates(projectDir, commands, { onGate })`, with the default timeout. The run is not stopped by a red gate; every selected gate runs.
- Error output: `gatesRunCommand` wraps steps 1-6 in one try/catch, like `workflowStatusCommand`, so any failure in any step (including an error thrown by `runQualityGates` mid-run, such as `assertTrusted` refusing inside `runQualityCommand`) returns 1 and is reported, and records of gates that already finished are discarded. Without `--json` the message lines go to stderr through `deps.logErr`, one call per line, with no prefix, and nothing goes to stdout. With `--json` stdout gets one line, `JSON.stringify({ error: message })`, where a two-line message (the untrusted case) is joined with `"; "`, and nothing goes to stderr. `guarded` (as in `src/cli/workflow.ts`) only catches what escapes that try/catch.
- Logging: `registerGatesCommand` does not call `initLogger`, so `runQualityCommand`'s log records never reach stdout and the `--json` single-document guarantee holds.
- Import cycles: `src/cli/gates.ts` imports `resolveGateCommands`, `runQualityGates` and the new types from `../finish/gates/quality` by relative path, not through the `@/finish` barrel, and does NOT import `src/workflow/repo-gates.ts`; `bun run check:import-cycles` must stay clean. `gateOutputTail` (US-001) supplies the 40-line tail.

Exit codes: 0 = at least one gate ran and every gate is `passed`; 1 = the command failed before reporting (no project, untrusted project, unreadable trust store, invalid config, unknown or unconfigured `--gate`, or any other thrown error); 2 = the gates were resolved and run and at least one is `failed`, `not-run` or `timed-out`, or no gate is configured at all (nothing was verified).

Plain output (stdout), one line per gate in run order, then the tail of each gate that did not pass, then a summary line:
```
passed     build      12.3s
failed     test       exit=1    48.0s
not-run    lint       exit=127  0.0s  (command not found or not executable; the gate did not run)
timed-out  e2e        900.0s

--- test (last 40 lines) ---
<outputTail>

--- lint (last 40 lines) ---
<outputTail>

--- e2e (last 40 lines) ---
<outputTail>

gates: 1 passed, 1 failed, 1 not run, 1 timed out
```
Every non-passed gate, `timed-out` included, gets a tail block. The column widths and duration format are illustrative and left to the builder. A gate line shows `exit=<n>` for every status except `passed` and `timed-out`; the `not-run` line always carries the same note, whatever the code (127, 126 or -1). A setup failure appends `(setup failed)` to its gate line. With nothing configured, plain output is the single line `no quality.commands configured in <projectDir>/.nax/config.json; nothing was verified`. `outputTail` is `gateOutputTail(record.output)`; an `output` that is empty after trimming gives an empty `outputTail` string, which is still present on a non-passed entry. A list-valued command reports the first non-zero exit code among its steps, so a list whose first step exits 127 is `not-run` even when a later step ran and failed.

`--json` example:
```json
{
  "projectDir": "/repo",
  "passed": false,
  "gates": [
    { "name": "build", "status": "passed", "exitCode": 0, "durationMs": 12300 },
    { "name": "lint", "status": "not-run", "exitCode": 127, "durationMs": 4, "outputTail": "/bin/sh: biome: command not found" }
  ],
  "summary": { "passed": 1, "failed": 0, "notRun": 1, "timedOut": 0 }
}
```

Failure handling: no `.nax/config.json` at or above `--dir` => exit 1, nothing loaded or spawned; untrusted project => exit 1 with the grant hint, fail-closed; trust store unreadable => exit 1 with the store error's message; invalid config (`resolveGateCommands` throws) => exit 1 with the thrown message; unknown or unconfigured `--gate` => exit 1, no gate runs; no gate configured => exit 2 with `passed: false`, `gates: []`; gate exits 127/126 or fails to spawn (-1, not timed out) => `not-run`, counted in `summary.notRun`, exit 2; gate times out => `timed-out`, exit 2; `e2e` setup fails => status is `classifyGateExit` of the setup result with `failedPhase: "setup"` and the `e2e` command is not run; a red gate => later gates still run, no retry.

**Scope** — In: `src/cli/gates.ts`, its registration in `bin/nax.ts` (verified by `bun run build`, `bun run typecheck` and `bun run check:import-cycles`, not by an AC), the `src/cli/index.ts` re-exports, and the cli-reference docs section. Out: changes to `runQualityGates`, `GateRunRecord`, `classifyGateExit`, `gateOutputTail` or `GATE_ORDER` themselves (US-001); package overlay gates, `*Fix`/`*Scoped` commands, `--profile`, `--timeout`, parallel runs, `nax workflow record|promote`.

**Interface**
```typescript
export interface GatesCliDeps {
  log: (msg: string) => void;
  logErr: (msg: string) => void;
  exit: (code: number) => void;
  isInteractive: () => boolean;
  ensureProjectTrusted: typeof ensureProjectTrusted;
  resolveGateCommands: typeof resolveGateCommands;
  runQualityGates: typeof runQualityGates;
}
export const _gatesCliDeps: GatesCliDeps;

export interface GatesRunOptions {
  readonly dir: string;
  /** Gate keys to run; empty means every configured root gate. */
  readonly gates: readonly string[];
  readonly json: boolean;
}

export interface GatesRunReport {
  /** Absolute project root the gates ran from. */
  readonly projectDir: string;
  /** True only when at least one gate ran and every gate is "passed". */
  readonly passed: boolean;
  readonly gates: readonly GateReportEntry[];
  readonly summary: { readonly passed: number; readonly failed: number; readonly notRun: number; readonly timedOut: number };
}

export interface GateReportEntry {
  readonly name: string;
  readonly status: GateRunStatus;
  readonly exitCode: number;
  readonly durationMs: number;
  readonly failedPhase?: "setup";
  /** `gateOutputTail(record.output)`; absent for a "passed" gate. */
  readonly outputTail?: string;
}

/** Runs the gates, prints the report, and returns the exit code. */
export function gatesRunCommand(opts: GatesRunOptions, deps?: GatesCliDeps): Promise<number>;

/** Registers `nax gates` with its `run` subcommand. */
export function registerGatesCommand(program: Command, deps?: GatesCliDeps): Command;
```

**Seams** — Consumes `runQualityGates`'s `onGate` callback and `classifyGateExit`'s statuses from US-001. Tests stub `runQualityGates` through `_gatesCliDeps` and drive `onGate` with `GateRunRecord`s; one test runs the real `runQualityGates` with a stubbed `_qualityGateDeps.run` so the exit code reaching the report comes from the runner.
